{Dear Champions! Before you go ahead please read the following 2 articles, on
how to work with this file and how to memorize the variations. https://
chessmood.com/blog/how-to-memorize-chess-openings-variations and https://
chessmood. com/blog/the-most-effective-way-to-create-chess-pgn-files I made a
draft file for you with homework. After you watch the course, I recommend to
add here all the things you've learned. Good luck!} 1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 {
What're the bishops we want to exchange?} Bd7 {The 3rd option and my
recommendation} (3... c5 4. c3 Nc6 (4... Qb6 5. Nf3 Bd7 {[%csl Gb5][%cal Gd7b5]
The 2nd option}) 5. Nf3 Qb6 {[%csl Rd4,Gf5][%cal Gg8f5] The 1st option}) 4. Nf3
(4. f4 {What's the downside of this move?}) 4... a6 5. Bd3 (5. c4 {How do we
face this move?}) (5. a4 {What's the downside of 5.a4? Why the a2 pawn's place
is on a3?}) (5. Nc3 c5 {[%csl Re5][%cal Gb8c6,Gc5d4]} 6. dxc5 Bxc5 7. Bd3 Nc6
8. O-O Nge7 {What's our plan? Do we castle short or long?}) 5... Bb5 6. O-O (6.
Bxb5+ axb5 7. O-O {Our plan is:} Ne7 8. Kh1 Nf5 9. Kg1 Nd7 10. Kh1 Nb6 11. Kg1
c6 12. Kh1 Be7 13. Kg1 Kd7 $1 14. Kh1 h5 15. Kg1 g5 16. Kh1 Qg8 17. Kg1 Qg6 {
[%csl Rg1][%cal Gh5h4,Gg5g4] [#]}) 6... Bxd3 (6... Ne7 $5) 7. Qxd3 Ne7 $1 {
My preference} (7... c5 8. c3 Nc6 9. Re1 cxd4 10. cxd4 Nge7 {[%csl Ge7,Gf5]
[%cal Ge7f5,Gf8e7]}) 8. Re1 Nf5 {The plan is:} 9. c3 Be7 (9... c5 $5) 10. Nbd2
Nc6 11. Nf1 h5 12. Bd2 g5 {[#]} *

